    "details": "<p><span role=\"text\"><strong data-start=\"3\" data-end=\"37\">Event Overview</strong></span></p>\n<p><strong data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"57\">OPTIQUEST 2026</strong> is a technical programming competition organized by the <strong data-start=\"114\" data-end=\"204\">Department of Computer Applications, R.V.R. &amp; J.C. College of Engineering (Autonomous)</strong>. Conducted as part of the department&rsquo;s <strong data-start=\"244\" data-end=\"262\">Technical Fest</strong> and associated with the <strong data-start=\"287\" data-end=\"300\">SWAA Club</strong>, the event is designed to challenge students&rsquo; programming knowledge, logical thinking, debugging skills, and problem-solving abilities.</p>\n<p>The competition brings together students from <strong data-start=\"484\" data-end=\"514\">B.Tech, M.Tech, and M.C.A.</strong> programs in teams of two, providing a platform to demonstrate their technical proficiency and compete through multiple levels of programming challenges.</p>\n<p><span role=\"text\"><strong data-start=\"673\" data-end=\"691\">Event Details:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"693\" data-end=\"931\">\n<li data-section-id=\"w5ic7r\" data-start=\"693\" data-end=\"734\"><strong data-start=\"695\" data-end=\"704\">Date:</strong> September 19, 2026 (Saturday)</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1l37c6d\" data-start=\"735\" data-end=\"782\"><strong data-start=\"737\" data-end=\"763\">Registration Deadline:</strong> September 18, 2026</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"unshj3\" data-start=\"783\" data-end=\"827\"><strong data-start=\"785\" data-end=\"806\">Team Composition:</strong> Teams of two members</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"5d34f5\" data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"889\"><strong data-start=\"830\" data-end=\"850\">Target Audience:</strong> Students of B.Tech, M.Tech, and M.C.A.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1pmx5rd\" data-start=\"890\" data-end=\"931\"><strong data-start=\"892\" data-end=\"902\">Venue:</strong> MCA Lab (MN-205), Main Block</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span role=\"text\"><strong data-start=\"937\" data-end=\"963\">Competition Structure:</strong></span></p>\n<p>The event consists of two rounds, progressing from fundamental programming knowledge to advanced coding and problem-solving challenges.</p>\n<p><span role=\"text\"><strong data-start=\"1106\" data-end=\"1148\">1. Prelims: Technical Proficiency Test</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1150\" data-end=\"1442\">\n<li data-section-id=\"lof5v0\" data-start=\"1150\" data-end=\"1186\"><strong data-start=\"1152\" data-end=\"1161\">Time:</strong> 10:30 A.M. to 12:00 P.M.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"88u6wq\" data-start=\"1187\" data-end=\"1233\"><strong data-start=\"1189\" data-end=\"1200\">Format:</strong> Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs)</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1ucvdr4\" data-start=\"1234\" data-end=\"1271\"><strong data-start=\"1236\" data-end=\"1247\">Topics:</strong> <strong data-start=\"1248\" data-end=\"1271\">C, Java, and Python</strong></li>\n<li data-section-id=\"129h0qa\" data-start=\"1272\" data-end=\"1319\"><strong data-start=\"1274\" data-end=\"1284\">Focus:</strong> Syntax, logic, and problem-solving</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"15vusx6\" data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"1442\"><strong data-start=\"1322\" data-end=\"1336\">Objective:</strong> To assess participants&rsquo; fundamental programming knowledge and identify the top teams for the final round.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span role=\"text\"><strong data-start=\"1448\" data-end=\"1480\">2. Mains: The Final Frontier</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1482\" data-end=\"1897\">\n<li data-section-id=\"16v8qn2\" data-start=\"1482\" data-end=\"1518\"><strong data-start=\"1484\" data-end=\"1493\">Time:</strong> 01:00 P.M. to 03:00 P.M.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"2lwco4\" data-start=\"1519\" data-end=\"1558\"><strong data-start=\"1521\" data-end=\"1532\">Format:</strong> Advanced coding challenge</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"10c3vw1\" data-start=\"1559\" data-end=\"1628\"><strong data-start=\"1561\" data-end=\"1577\">Eligibility:</strong> Only the top-performing teams from Round 1 qualify</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1meqg0m\" data-start=\"1629\" data-end=\"1734\"><strong data-start=\"1631\" data-end=\"1654\">Challenges Include:</strong>\n<ul data-start=\"1657\" data-end=\"1734\">\n<li data-section-id=\"h7veby\" data-start=\"1657\" data-end=\"1685\">Advanced Coding Challenges</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"6h8973\" data-start=\"1688\" data-end=\"1707\">Debugging Sprints</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"hsd7xi\" data-start=\"1710\" data-end=\"1734\">Algorithm Optimization</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1a4w34f\" data-start=\"1735\" data-end=\"1897\"><strong data-start=\"1737\" data-end=\"1751\">Objective:</strong> To test participants&rsquo; ability to solve complex programming problems efficiently and apply their technical knowledge under competitive conditions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span role=\"text\"><strong data-start=\"1903\" data-end=\"1931\">Rewards and Recognition:</strong></span></p>\n<p>The event offers cash prizes to the top three teams:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1987\" data-end=\"2209\">\n<li data-section-id=\"ssw6qn\" data-start=\"1987\" data-end=\"2017\"><strong data-start=\"1989\" data-end=\"2005\">First Prize:</strong> Rs. 2,000/-</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"13fgsfn\" data-start=\"2018\" data-end=\"2049\"><strong data-start=\"2020\" data-end=\"2037\">Second Prize:</strong> Rs. 1,500/-</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1u9ty05\" data-start=\"2050\" data-end=\"2080\"><strong data-start=\"2052\" data-end=\"2068\">Third Prize:</strong> Rs. 1,000/-</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"17kr5on\" data-start=\"2081\" data-end=\"2209\"><strong data-start=\"2083\" data-end=\"2099\">Recognition:</strong> Certificates of Merit will be awarded to all participants who qualify for and participate in the Final Round.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span role=\"text\"><strong data-start=\"2215\" data-end=\"2245\">Registration &amp; Eligibility</strong></span></p>\n<p>Students from <strong data-start=\"2261\" data-end=\"2291\">B.Tech, M.Tech, and M.C.A.</strong> programs are eligible to participate. Each team must consist of <strong data-start=\"2356\" data-end=\"2371\">two members</strong>. Participants are required to register before the <strong data-start=\"2422\" data-end=\"2444\">September 18, 2026</strong> deadline.</p>\n<p><span role=\"text\"><strong data-start=\"2460\" data-end=\"2485\">Organizing Leadership</strong></span></p>\n<p>The event is organized by the <strong data-start=\"2517\" data-end=\"2607\">Department of Computer Applications, R.V.R. &amp; J.C. College of Engineering (Autonomous)</strong>, in association with the <strong data-start=\"2633\" data-end=\"2646\">SWAA Club</strong>.</p>",
